Unfortunately I can't use `str` + `pad_zeroes`, because that would significantly worsen usage of the function (it's a library function, user can pass a format string for specific numbers). For now I added a hack for default format string (just `.replace(" ", "0")`).

> Does the printf "standard" have a way to pad a number with spaces?

Yes, without the `0` in a format string: 
```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
	printf("<%7.2f>\n", 0.123);
}

---
<   0.12>
```
I believe for integers Godot's `%` operator [behaves same](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/getting_started/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_format_string.html#padding) as `printf` (without `0` spaces, with `0` zeroes).
